From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:13:28 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] ASoC: qcom: x1e80100: run the speakers at their DT operating
 point

The card keeps the WSA speakers at -3 dB digital gain with the PA at
its floor, about 0.7 V peak on the HP OmniBook Ultra 14, far below what
they take with protection running. The DT operating point only holds
on the gain path it was measured on, and SP VI must model the same
full scale.

When speaker protection is required and every amplifier has an
operating point and the V/I guard, set up that path at late probe
instead of the default limits: each interpolator fed only from its own
AIF1 input, compander and soft clip off, 0 dB digital gain, amplifiers
in speaker mode at their PA ceiling. Each control is set, read back and
made read-only before userspace can reach it, a failure fails the card,
and the full scale is passed to audioreach. A read-only "Speaker
Operating Point Switch" shows whether this is active.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 sound/soc/qcom/x1e80100.c | 199 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 195 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/x1e80100.c b/sound/soc/qcom/x1e80100.c
index cefac8b97ad5..9163c9563cfb 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/x1e80100.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/x1e80100.c
@@ -19,12 +19,27 @@
